--TEST--
`Core\Response\Stream::write` sends octets no text-shaped chunk could carry, and a body written in chunks is byte-for-byte the body written whole -- `rule:concurrency/a-stream-that-outlives-its-request-is-a-connection` and `rule:types/bytes`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Response\Stream::write
// The `bytes` arm of the one parameter, asked the question `text` cannot be
// asked: a chunk holding a NUL, control bytes and a byte that is not valid
// UTF-8 goes out unchanged. The parent reads each body back with
// `Core\Test::request`, whose response keeps the body as bytes. A capture
// cannot read it: it throws for bytes that are not UTF-8, and it replaces
// control bytes.
if (Core\Env::context() == Core\Env::Context::Request) {
    var $path = Core\Request::path();
    if ($path == "/chunks") {
        var $image = Core\Response::stream("image/png");
        $image->write(Core\Encoding::fromHex("504e470d0a1a0a"));
        $image->write(Core\Encoding::fromHex("00"));
    }
    if ($path == "/chunks-ff") {
        var $octets = Core\Response::stream("image/png");
        $octets->write(Core\Encoding::fromHex("504e470d0a1a0a"));
        $octets->write(Core\Encoding::fromHex("00ff"));
    }
    if ($path == "/whole-ff") {
        Core\Response::bytes(Core\Encoding::fromHex("504e470d0a1a0a00ff"), "image/png");
    }
    if ($path == "/rows-whole") {
        Core\Response::text("id,name\n1,ada\n2,alan\n");
    }
    if ($path == "/rows-chunked") {
        var $rows = Core\Response::stream("text/plain; charset=utf-8");
        $rows->write("id,name\n");
        $rows->write("1,ada\n");
        $rows->write("2,alan\n");
    }
} else {
    // The NUL and the control bytes are valid UTF-8, so `body()` returns them,
    // and the hex is the hex the two chunks sent.
    var $chunks = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/chunks");
    echo $chunks->header("Content-Type") ?? "none", " ", Core\Encoding::toHex($chunks->body() as bytes), "\n";

    // The same octets and then `FF`. `body()` throws at byte 8, so the first
    // eight octets arrived unchanged and `FF` arrived as itself.
    string $streamed = "";
    try {
        Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/chunks-ff")->body();
    } catch (RuntimeError $notText) {
        $streamed = $notText->message;
    }
    echo $streamed, "\n";

    // Agreement, which is the claim a member answering plausibly on its own
    // line would still fail: the same body written whole and written in pieces
    // is the same bytes. For the octets the two errors name the same byte, and
    // for text the two bodies are equal. A stream that dropped, reordered or
    // padded a chunk fails here while each half still reads correctly alone.
    string $whole = "";
    try {
        Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/whole-ff")->body();
    } catch (RuntimeError $wholeNotText) {
        $whole = $wholeNotText->message;
    }
    string $rowsWhole = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/rows-whole")->body();
    string $rowsChunked = Core\Test::request(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/rows-chunked")->body();
    if ($streamed == $whole && $rowsWhole == $rowsChunked && $rowsWhole == "id,name\n1,ada\n2,alan\n") {
        echo "agree\n";
    } else {
        echo "differ\n";
    }
}
--EXPECT--
image/png 504e470d0a1a0a00
Core\Test\Response::body(): the response body is not valid UTF-8 at byte 8, so it is not a string. Use `status()` and `header()` to test this response.
agree
